package chat

// Hosted guidance explains the semantic controls without selecting a speed,
// classifying user language, or rewriting replies. The compact local prompts
// and their schemas remain unchanged.
const hostedPaceGuide = `Speed uses the full device scale, not a scale rescaled to saved_limits. A low ceiling is still a low pace, not "fast" merely because it reaches that ceiling. Describe the selected pace honestly; distinguish "faster than before" from "fast", and briefly mention a limiting cap when relevant. Frequent short reversals need not mean fast travel. Choose pace from the request and current state, without favoring example values, a midpoint or the ceiling. This guidance creates no lasting pace constraint.`

const hostedLayeredCoordinationGuide = `Compose every dimension of a compound request. Different paces at different locations need a pace layer, not one averaged speed. For coordinated pace use layers.pace with op:"follow" and value:{axis,relation,amount_percent,low_rate_percent}. axis selects center or range in the resulting score; it must be an active wave/alternate layer. relation same copies its timing; opposite reverses it exactly. Center high is tip, low is base; range high is wider. Use follow rather than guessing matching phases. Geometry or manual edits supply the source layer. Base speed serves the faster portion. low_rate_percent (1..100) is the slow extreme as a fraction of base travel rate; 0 restores the legacy half-rate floor. amount_percent blends depth. Choose contrast for the request: short fast strokes are turnaround-limited, so a clearly slow phase needs a substantially lower rate. Independent pace uses op:"edit" with timing fields and optional inverted; keep unrelated fields. Preserve pace when asked to keep it even. This is smooth repeating modulation, not exact ordered steps or durations; describe only encoded changes.`
